        <detaileddescription>
<para>Construct a token.</para><para>The token has the specified type and its lexeme are the characters at the specified position in the input stream. The <computeroutput>begin</computeroutput> points to the first character of the lexeme and <computeroutput>end</computeroutput> points to one past the last character. <ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref> token&apos;s lexeme is allowed to be the empty string by specifying the same value for <computeroutput>begin</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>end</computeroutput>, however, <computeroutput>end</computeroutput> must never be less than <computeroutput>begin</computeroutput>. </para>        </detaileddescription>
