        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Lexer_1_1Token" kindref="compound">Token</ref> lexeme ending position.</para><para>This is the offset in the input for one position past the last character of this token&apos;s lexeme. It is guaranteed to be greater than or equal to the <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Lexer_1_1Token_1afaa99c2b05484bf33c3a19cb4d39b330" kindref="member">begin</ref> position. EOF tokens will always have a <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Lexer_1_1Token_1afaa99c2b05484bf33c3a19cb4d39b330" kindref="member">begin</ref> equal to the <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Lexer_1_1Token_1a4485336cfa4855cb82ab29bd7fe225bd" kindref="member">end</ref>, but other empty non-EOF tokens are also possible. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/home/liao6/workspace/rose-github/src/Sawyer/Lexer.h" line="81" column="1" bodyfile="/home/liao6/workspace/rose-github/src/Sawyer/Lexer.h" bodystart="81" bodyend="83"/>
      </memberdef>
